                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "During the visit, KU students had the opportunity to speak with Director Bhattacharya and tell him about their research. I appreciate the support from the NIH for the KU Health System, as it invests in the success of KS students and future medical researchers, doctors and health professionals. These individuals will play a critical role in the ongoing effort to find cures for diseases that impact many lives.\n\nThank you to @DrJBhattacharya for taking the time to visit & learn more about the incredible research being conducted right here in KS. Thank you to Chancellor Girod, Dr. Roy Jensen, and the entire team\u2014as well as the advocacy leaders & Kansas representatives who joined us\u2014for their hospitality and for their commitment to improving health outcomes across Kansas and the country.",
