                "reply_count": 16,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "It was great to tour Russell Regional Hospital and speak with hospital leadership about their efforts to provide critical health care to the community. We also discussed the recently announced $222 million awarded to Kansas through the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services Rural Health Transformation Program to invest in and improve outcomes for rural hospitals. Thank you to Director of Human Resources Stephanie Flegler and Director of Communications Janae Talbott for hosting me. I also appreciated Russell County Commission Chair Duke Strobel, Russell Mayor Jim Cross, Russell Economic Development Director Mike Parsons and City Council President Dustin Madden joining me on my tour.",
